+# swscale candidate — implementation notes
+
+Build: `zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseFast` (target pinned to x86-64-v3 in `build.zig`).
+
+## Layout
+- `src/main.zig` — exact scalar port of FFmpeg's (C, `--disable-asm`) swscale behaviour for the
+  formats in the contract: filter construction (`initFilter`), yuv->rgb tables, rgb->yuv
+  coefficients, the generic pipeline (input conversion -> horizontal filter into 15-bit
+  intermediates -> vertical filter/output) and the unscaled special converters FFmpeg picks
+  (yuv2rgb tables, rgb shuffles, planar<->NV12, bgr24->yv12). It is bit-exact against the reference.
+- `src/fast.zig` — `@Vector` SIMD kernels. Every hook returns `false` when it does not apply, and
+  the scalar code in `main.zig` runs instead. All kernels are integer-exact emulations of the scalar
+  arithmetic (e.g. the yuv->rgb table lookup is reproduced with a mulhi-based formula).
+- `tools/prof.py` — per-opcode cost histogram of one conversion (`python3 tools/prof.py b000`).
+- `tools/sizes.py` — checks all contract pairs/algorithms at other frame sizes against the reference.
+
+## FFmpeg behaviours that matter for exactness
+- GRAY8 is treated as full range (`handle_jpeg`), so YUV<->GRAY goes through the generic path with
+  luma range conversion; gray->RGB uses full-range yuv2rgb tables.
+- RGB sources force full-chroma output (`SWS_FULL_CHR_H_INT`); RGB inputs use the "half" chroma
+  input when `dstW >> chrDstHSub <= srcW >> 1`.
+- Packed output picks yuv2packed1/2/X by filter sizes; packed1 with a 2-tap chroma filter averages
+  the two chroma lines only when the second coefficient is >= 2048.
+- Horizontal scaling only runs for source rows the vertical filter uses.
